{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_transcription_pack", "label": "Transcription pack \u2014 the writing-only rows with their numbers", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every figure is lifted from a committed artefact and carries its source path, so Phase 8 is transcription, not derivation."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_tab_winkler", "label": "tab:winkler \u2014 Winkler, coverage, Clopper-Pearson, width", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The intervals were already computed and stored as cp_lo/cp_hi; the caption promised them and the table simply never printed them."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_clopper_pearson_intervals", "label": "Clopper-Pearson coverage intervals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The interval is what makes the Beer Hall under-coverage and the Two River Taps over-coverage sayable rather than a phrase."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_d_f3", "label": "D-F3 \u2014 the interval columns that were never printed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_d_f4", "label": "D-F4 \u2014 tab:ladder dispersion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_w36", "label": "Weakness W36 \u2014 the single named reason Distinction is 'Not met'", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The statistics were never missing: sd, se and n are on the page for every rung. A gap of one-fifth of a standard error is not a result, and bolding a winner across it is the defect W36 names."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_ask_f1_cost_sweep", "label": "The Ask-F1 / cost sweep degeneracy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ledger row was wrong in both limbs: there are 124 misses, not zero, and cost rises 132.0 to 1248.0, not flat. The degeneracy is real but one-sided toward misses rather than the over-offering the row assumed."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_d_f5", "label": "D-F5 \u2014 state the degeneracy as our instance", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_retrieval_threat_model", "label": "Threat model for the retrieval store", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/transcription_pack.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three properties bound the exposure: single-tenant corpus so the attacker must already be staff, a briefing a named human reads rather than an autonomous actuator, and a forecast path that does not read the retrieval store at all. No mitigation is implemented and none is claimed; the exposure is stated because an unstated one is worse."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_transcription_pack_d_f6", "label": "D-F6 \u2014 retrieval threat model", 